  "body": "I am reviewing [a PR](https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/pull/771) which uses an infra map whose keys are structs. If one were to enumerate the map and print all values, in what order should the map entries be iterated over? A \"struct\" isn't a primitive, so it doesn't have any obvious default comparison operators. Should we make people provide their own? Or should map keys not be allowed to be structs, and instead be restricted to [primitive types](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#primitive-data-types)? Even if we did the latter, we'd still have to deal with ordered sets, which are just lists with [\"items\"](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-item), and we certainly can't restrict _all_ \"items\" to primitives. (Maybe we could just for _ordered set_ items?).",
